<%= @title %>

A refresh token for the GitHub App "<%= @app_name %>", that is linked to your GitHub account - @<%= @user.display_login %>, was reported to GitHub through GitHub's credential revocation API: <%= "#{GitHub.help_url}/rest/credentials/revoke#revoke-a-list-of-credentials" %>

To protect your data from unauthorized access, we have revoked this token to ensure that it can no longer be used to authenticate to GitHub on your behalf: <%= "#{GitHub.help_url}/authentication/keeping-your-account-and-data-secure/token-expiration-and-revocation" %>

To encourage reports and ensure that exposed tokens can be quickly and easily revoked, we do not require authentication for submissions. As a result, GitHub is unable to provide further information about the source of the reported token.

If you did not submit this token to GitHub's credential revocation API and you believe that your token was exposed, you can review your security log to ensure that unauthorized activity has not occurred using this token: <%= settings_user_audit_log_url %>
To learn more about reviewing your security log, visit our help docs: <%= "#{GitHub.help_url}/authentication/keeping-your-account-and-data-secure/reviewing-your-security-log"%>

To restore access to this application, you will need to re-authorize by logging in to the application again. You can view your authorized GitHub Apps in your GitHub settings: <%= @authorized_apps_url %>
